  "summary": "Flock Safety CEO Garrett Langley issues a statement responding to reporting about Flock LPR misuse and federal cooperation. He disputes characterizations of a Johnson County, TX search as targeting abortion-seekers, defends local agency discretion to cooperate with federal authorities, and describes Flock's sharing options (1:1, National Lookup), audit features, and new compliance tools including Illinois policy attestation and proactive search-term filtering.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "According to the Sheriff in Johnson County himself, this claim is unequivocally false.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "This was not a \"back door\" into Flock, as some in the media have claimed \u2014 these cases and many others represent active choices, within the boundaries of the law, made by local police",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    },
    {
      "quote": "Some states, like California, do not allow any sharing across state borders. For those states, Flock has disabled National Lookup to make compliance easier.",
      "paragraph_idx": 21
    },
    {
      "quote": "every single search conducted in the Flock LPR system is saved in an audit report",
      "paragraph_idx": 24
    }
  ],
